WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.262
This is a brief: one ad idea, and everything your editor needs to make it.

2
00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:14.331
Up top are the status, the brand, the strategist, the editor and the due date. Click any of them to change it.

3
00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:18.989
The angle is the idea: who it's for, and why they'll care.

4
00:00:19.139 --> 00:00:21.814
The test is what you want to learn.

5
00:00:21.964 --> 00:00:28.156
Pick what changes between the ads, here the creator, and everything else stays the same.

6
00:00:28.306 --> 00:00:33.209
That way, when results come in, Folio knows what made the difference.

7
00:00:33.359 --> 00:00:40.079
Notes for the editor and references come next: footage, pacing, links and images.

8
00:00:40.229 --> 00:00:45.930
Each variation is one ad, with its own hook, body and call to action.

9
00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:51.920
Copy ad name gives you the name to use in Meta, so results come back to this brief.

10
00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:56.746
Below are your past winners for this brand, so you can build on what worked.

11
00:00:56.896 --> 00:00:59.702
On the right, your team leaves comments.

12
00:00:59.852 --> 00:01:04.424
And the AI tab can draft the brief, or improve a section for you.

13
00:01:04.574 --> 00:01:10.980
Prefer a visual board? Canvas lays out the hooks, body and call to action as cards.

14
00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:16.570
When it's ready, click Share to send it to your editor. They don't need an account.

15
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.793
Watch this again any time from this menu.
